ist":"Hogweard","license":"Public domain","url":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Leicestershire.svg"},"story":"The flag of Leicestershire is the flag of the historic county of Leicestershire, England. It was registered with the Flag Institute on 16 July 2021. Leicestershire was the last English county to have a registered flag.","story_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag_of_Leicestershire"},{"id":"q23098","q":"Q23098","name":"Derbyshire","region":"East Midlands","country":"United Kingdom","kind":"division","type":"Ceremonial county","lat":53.18,"lon":-1.61,"pop":1056000,"about":"Ceremonial county in East Midlands, England","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derbyshire","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Derbyshire_flag.svg/330px-Derbyshire_flag.svg.png","src":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Derbyshire_flag.svg?width=960","credit":{"artist":"Dyfsunctional at English Wikipedia","license":"Public domain","url":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Derbyshire_flag.svg"},"story":"The flag of Derbyshire is the flag of the English county of Derbyshire. Created in 2006, the flag has subsequently been registered at the Flag Institute and added to their UK Flags Register.","story_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag_of_Derbyshire"},{"id":"q23157","q":"Q23157","name":"Somerset","region":"South West England","country":"United Kingdom","kind":"division","type":"Ceremonial county","lat":51.3,"lon":-3.0,"pop":975782,"about":"Ceremonial county of England (use Q21694741 for administrative non-metropolitan county)","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Somerset","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Somerset_Flag.svg/330px-Somerset_Flag.svg.png","src":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Somerset_Flag.svg?width=960","credit":{"artist":"User:Hogweard","license":"Public domain","url":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Somerset_Flag.svg"}},{"id":"q23220","q":"Q23220","name":"Berkshire","region":"South East England","country":"United Kingdom","kind":"division","type":"Ceremonial county","lat":51.42,"lon":-1.0,"pop":917762,"about":"Ceremonial and non-metropolitan but non-administrative county of England","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berkshire","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Flag_of_Berkshire.svg/330px-Flag_of_Berkshire.svg.png","src":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Flag_of_Berkshire.svg?width=960","credit":{"artist":"The Flag Institute Vexilo Hogweard","license":"Public domain","url":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Berkshire.svg"},"story":"The Flag of Berkshire is the flag of the historic county of Berkshire in England. The flag was registered with the Flag Institute as the flag of the county in March 2017. The flag was adopted after the design was submitted by a number of county-based bodies as well as the Lord Lieutenant of the county.","story_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag_of_Berkshire"},{"id":"q23109","q":"Q23109","name":"Norfolk","region":"East of England","country":"United Kingdom","kind":"division","type":"Ceremonial county","lat":52.6725,"lon":0.95,"pop":914039,"about":"County in East Anglia, England, UK","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norfolk","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Flag_of_Norfolk.svg/330px-Flag_of_Norfolk.svg.png","src":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Flag_of_Norfolk.svg?width=960","credit":{"artist":"Hogweard","license":"Public domain","url":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Norfolk.svg"},"story":"The flag of the English county of Norfolk consists of a vertical bi-colour of gold and black, with a white bend bearing nine black ermine spots alternating between pairs and singles.","story_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag_of_Norfolk"},{"id":"q23287","q":"Q23287","name":"West